WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.062
Welcome to Little Newtons! Let's explore tens and ones.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.559
Look at thirty-four. The three is in the tens place. The four is in the ones place.

3
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.002
Here are ten single blocks. Watch them come together. Ten ones make one ten.

4
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.353
Each green rod is one ten. Count by tens.

5
00:00:25.853 --> 00:00:26.283
Ten.

6
00:00:26.783 --> 00:00:27.317
Twenty.

7
00:00:27.817 --> 00:00:28.293
Thirty.

8
00:00:28.793 --> 00:00:30.384
Three tens make thirty.

9
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.935
Each gold block is one. Let's count.

10
00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:35.691
One.

11
00:00:36.191 --> 00:00:36.586
Two.

12
00:00:37.086 --> 00:00:37.399
Three.

13
00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:38.294
Four.

14
00:00:38.794 --> 00:00:40.454
Four ones make four.

15
00:00:41.758 --> 00:00:49.688
Thirty plus four equals thirty-four! Three tens and four ones make thirty-four. The place tells us each digit's value.

16
00:00:51.008 --> 00:00:56.453
Your turn! Look at twenty-six. How many tens? How many ones? Pause and think.

17
00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:07.293
Twenty-six has two tens and six ones. Twenty plus six equals twenty-six. Great thinking!
